# .clinerules - Next.js Frontend Excellence

## Core Principles
- Prioritize user experience and accessibility (WCAG AA minimum)
- Write clean, maintainable, and type-safe code
- Follow Next.js 13+ App Router best practices
- Implement performance optimization automatically

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript with strict mode enabled
- Follow ESLint and Prettier configurations
- Component-driven architecture with atomic design
- Proper error handling and loading states

## Next.js Best Practices
- Optimize images with next/image
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use Server Components by default, Client Components when needed
- Route protection and middleware for auth
- SEO optimization (meta tags, structured data, sitemap)

## UX/UI Excellence
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, ARIA labels, keyboard navigation
- Fast Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
- Dark mode support consideration
- Loading skeletons and transitions

## Performance
- Code splitting and lazy loading
- Optimize bundles with dynamic imports
- Font optimization and preloading
- Image optimization strategies
- CSS minimization

## File Organization